WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:05.743
Government teams work across policy, implementation guidance, standards,
governance minutes and decision records.

00:05.743 --> 00:14.454
Before advice is submitted or assurance is given, reviewers need the
authoritative source, the current wording and a clear route back

00:14.454 --> 00:15.698
to the evidence.

00:15.698 --> 00:22.750
When that trail is fragmented, skilled people spend time reconstructing
documentary context instead of judging the issue.

00:23.750 --> 00:31.590
A policy question can depend on the current policy, earlier wording,
implementation guidance, a standard, governance minutes and a

00:31.590 --> 00:32.415
recorded decision.

00:32.415 --> 00:34.478
A reference can be replaced.

00:34.478 --> 00:36.954
A date can change what applied.

00:36.954 --> 00:40.668
Local guidance may narrow how a policy is implemented.

00:40.668 --> 00:43.144
The challenge is not simply search.

00:43.144 --> 00:47.270
It is establishing authority, chronology and the relationships between
sources.

00:48.270 --> 00:53.716
Choose one unclassified or appropriately controlled policy estate and one
review workflow.

00:53.716 --> 01:00.070
Agree the corpus, users, access boundary, test questions and evidence standard
before evaluation begins.

01:00.070 --> 01:05.970
Include stale references, incomplete records, conflicting wording and
questions that should be refused.

01:05.970 --> 01:11.870
Compare matched tasks against the current process, with authorised officials
adjudicating the results.

01:12.870 --> 01:18.704
Cortessa is intended to operate on a dedicated sovereign workstation inside an
agreed boundary.

01:18.704 --> 01:24.538
The approved corpus, local index, on-device model and source viewer remain
within that environment.

01:24.538 --> 01:28.705
Runtime operation does not depend on a public cloud service.

01:28.705 --> 01:33.289
The department defines permitted information, users, identity controls and
security posture.

01:33.289 --> 01:40.790
Cortessa does not bypass handling rules or automatically make material
suitable for OFFICIAL, SECRET or any other classification.

01:41.790 --> 01:44.843
Audit is the centre of the Cortessa workflow.

01:44.843 --> 01:53.239
Across the bounded policy estate, it can surface a policy that cites a missing
standard, guidance that appears to rely on superseded

01:53.239 --> 01:58.200
wording, inconsistent terminology, uncertain effectivity or an unexplained gap
in the decision record.

01:58.200 --> 02:00.872
Each candidate enters an authorised review queue.

02:00.872 --> 02:05.070
It is not automatically a finding of legal or administrative non-compliance.

02:06.070 --> 02:10.535
Each audit result leads back to the passage that created it.

02:10.535 --> 02:17.029
The authorised reviewer can open the source, inspect surrounding wording and
confirm document state and chronology.

02:17.029 --> 02:21.899
If evidence is absent, Cortessa can refuse rather than fill the gap.

02:21.899 --> 02:29.205
The accountable official determines relevance, accepts or rejects the
candidate, and records the outcome through the existing process.

02:29.205 --> 02:33.670
Verified shows provenance; it does not establish policy correctness or
authority.

02:34.670 --> 02:42.037
Democratic accountability, statutory duties, policy intent and operational
context cannot be delegated to a language model.

02:42.037 --> 02:45.720
Cortessa can expose the evidence route and uncertainty.

02:45.720 --> 02:52.166
Accountable officials determine what applies, what it means and what
recommendation should be made.

02:52.166 --> 02:57.230
Cortessa does not take ministerial, policy, procurement, statutory or
regulatory decisions.

02:58.230 --> 03:04.768
Reviewers need the source route, document state and the policy governing what
the system may present.

03:04.768 --> 03:09.263
Identity, document currency, assertion policy and egress posture remain
visible concerns.

03:09.263 --> 03:17.026
Local activity can be recorded in a ledger so the organisation can inspect
what the system did and when.

03:17.026 --> 03:23.973
That record can support an assurance package, but it does not guarantee
compliance with security, records-management or

03:23.973 --> 03:24.790
freedom-of-information obligations.

03:25.790 --> 03:29.372
Compare matched tasks against the current review workflow.

03:29.372 --> 03:36.088
Measure time to the authoritative source, traceability, stale-revision
visibility, accepted and rejected findings, correct refusals,

03:36.088 --> 03:37.878
reviewer effort and reproducibility.

03:37.878 --> 03:40.565
Record corpus preparation and setup burden.

03:40.565 --> 03:43.699
Include ambiguous policy language and absent records.

03:43.699 --> 03:51.310
The result should show where Cortessa helps, where it fails and what must
change before any expansion.

03:52.310 --> 03:58.099
Bring one appropriately controlled policy estate and the people authorised to
judge it.

03:58.099 --> 04:03.443
Evaluate the evidence route, remediate observed gaps and retest before
considering expansion.

04:03.443 --> 04:05.670
Start a conversation with Cortessa.
